    "name": "Patrick Audley"
  },
  "body": "The Turtle renderer recurses once per nested blank-node level when it packs `[ \u2026 ]` property lists. A long blank-node chain, such as a long RDF collection built by hand or a deep `[ ex:p [ ex:p \u2026 ] ]`, can exhaust the native stack, and there is a related pack-depth limit. The owner ruled that the deep-chain guard stays permanently. What remains is to make the renderer stack-safe (an explicit work list, not recursion) and its pack-depth handling correct and deterministic.\n\nRequired: Turtle and TriG output over 10^5- and 10^6-deep blank-node chains completes natively and on wasm32, byte-identically. Shallow chains keep their packed output. Add a bench.",
